images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scml6e.jpg"}], "slug": "double-dragon-advance", "storyline": "Martial arts masters Billy and Jimmy Lee set out to rescue Billy's girlfriend Marian after she is abducted by the ruthless street gang known as the Shadow Warriors. Fighting through city streets, a treacherous Chinatown, cavern depths, and an enemy fortress, the brothers battle the gang's toughest members and rival martial artists standing between them and her. Whether facing the onslaught alone or side by side, the Lee brothers must punch, kick, and grapple their way to the gang's stronghold to bring Marian home.", "summary": "Double Dragon Advance is a side-scrolling beat 'em up game developed by Million and published by Atlus for the Game Boy Advance. Released in 2003, it serves as an enhanced remake of the original Double Dragon arcade game, incorporating elements from the entire Double Dragon series.\n\nThe game follows brothers Billy and Jimmy Lee as they battle through various stages to rescue Marian from a dangerous gang. It features new levels, enemies, and moves not found in the original version, along with improved graphics and expanded combat mechanics.", "themes": [{"id": 1, "name": "Action"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/double-dragon-advance", "collections": [{"id": 694, "name": "Double Dragon"}]}